diagnostics: pin the resolved face's own body, pair bodies by their faces

Three holes, all of the same species: the probe could certify something it
had not checked.

1. `diff_resolution` ignored WHICH body the reference resolved into.
   91247A720's three raised grade marks are congruent separate bodies, so a
   reference that drifted to another mark's corresponding face matches on
   area, box and surface type -- the probe would have reported a broken
   reference as healthy. `resolve_census` now records the owning body of
   the resolved face (`IFace2.GetBody` -> `GetBodyBox`) and the verdict
   requires it to match the stored one. Bodies are compared by EXTENTS, not
   by name: a body name comes from the feature that made it and is not
   something this rewrite promises to preserve. A resolved face whose owner
   was not recorded reads as "proves nothing", not as a pass.

2. The body pairing used the persistent-reference multiset as its exact
   pass. Those bytes are allowed to change on rebuild, so for two bodies
   with equal extents -- congruent marks, a mirrored pair -- it would
   routinely find no exact partner and fall back to enumeration order.
   Where such bodies differ in their FACES, that mispairing reported both
   as having swapped faces, out of nothing. It now disambiguates on the
   sorted face-geometry multiset; extents alone remain the fallback, so a
   body that really did change a face is still paired and diagnosed.

3. The raw-primitive audit collects files with `rglob` but excluded them by
   `path.name`, so a same-named file in any subdirectory of `diagnostics`
   would have been exempt silently -- an exemption nobody wrote and nobody
   would see. Exemptions are now keyed by path relative to the diagnostics
   directory, and the companion staleness test builds the path the same
   way.

Verification:
- uv run python -m pytest cad/scripts/test_face_identity_diff.py
  cad/scripts/test_sketch_preference_baseline.py
  cad/scripts/test_logo_profile_closure.py -> 65 passed
- New cases: a reference landing in another body is reported; a resolved
  face with no owning body recorded proves nothing; congruent bodies whose
  faces differ pair by their faces. The last one returns exactly the two
  false "face area 4.0 -> 9.0 / 9.0 -> 4.0" lines under the old
  persist-based exact pass, confirmed by substituting it back in.
- uv run ruff check / ruff format --check -> clean
